<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara Malaysia governor reappointed to post.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara Malaysia governor reappointed to post.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The governor of Bank Negara Malaysia Ahmad Mohamed Don has been reappointed as head of the central bank until April 30, 2000, the national Bernama news agency reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Ahmad, a British-trained economist, was reappointed to the post before the expiry of his current three-year term on April 30, Bernama quoted a statement from the finance minister's office as saying.</p>
<p>Ahmad is also chairman of national mortgage corporation Cagamas, the Asean Finance Corporation Ltd and Malaysia Export Credit Insurance.</p>
<p>He was made govenor of Bank Negara in 1994.</p>
</text>
